The Yocto Project team is pleased to announce Yocto Project Developer
Day at the Congress Centre in D=C3=BCsseldorf, October 16th, 2014. This
year we have new workshop sessions divided into two separate tracks
(introductory and advanced). You can attend the session that fits your
level of knowledge around using the Yocto Project tools. We also give
you the opportunity to choose a development board to work on during
the hands-on portion of the day =E2=80=93 and you get to keep the board!
Registration is now available when you register for the Embedded Linux
Conference Europe (ELCE), or you can register separately if you aren't
planning to attend ELCE. Be sure to pick a board to use in the
classroom and take home with you.

We have a lineup of skilled trainers ready to teach you firsthand how
to download and use Yocto Project=E2=80=99s open source, high-quality
infrastructure and tools in order to build your own custom Linux
distributions across multiple architectures.

QUICK LINKS:

Event description (including agenda):
https://www.yoctoproject.org/tools-resources/events/yocto-project-developer=
-day-elce-2014

Extend your Embedded Linux Conference experience:
http://events.linuxfoundation.org/events/embedded-linux-conference-europe/e=
xtend-the-experience/yocto-dev-day

Register today and use the early registration discount rates:
https://www.regonline.com/Register/Checkin.aspx?EventID=3D1585929

Our speakers have years of practical experience so you can get your
answers and advance your knowledge in building a Yocto Project
compatible platform on the board that you chose.

Register today and save up to $50 off onsite prices. Please feel free
to pass the news to other Yocto Project enthusiasts. You will be sure
to find the right tutorials, experts, workshops and boards ready for
Yocto Project enablement.

Why should this matter to you? If you are anything like other open
source dedicated developers you will appreciate the facilities Yocto
Project is providing. So tap into the wonders of open source
innovation by:

- Learning how to maximize use of the Yocto Project tools, including
the Poky build system, Toaster and many more

- Selecting a silicon board for a hands-on build, and keeping
everything in the end

- Board choices: BeagleBone Black, WandBoard Quad, MinnowBoard Max

- Getting training sessions for all levels, Yocto Project beginners
and advanced developers

If you need more answers or have any trouble, please contact Jefro,
the community manager, at jefro@jefro.net.

See you in Dusseldorf!

